{{- /*
model/entity.go renders one entity's model declarations: the struct a
scanned row fills and a handler marshals, one generated type plus one
constant per member for each enum field, and -- since hooks (step 6)
cannot type-check without them, spec §10's amended step 6 row -- the
CreateInput/UpdateInput structs spec §6.5 projects from the same field set
(spec §5.6's model row).

Nearly logic-free, per spec §5.1: every Go type, every identifier and every
quoted literal comes from the IR or from a funcMap function in gen.go. The
only control flow here is iteration over slices the IR already orders --
never a map, whose iteration order Go randomises (spec §5.3) -- and the two
if blocks selecting whether an input type exists at all
(HasCreate/HasUpdate), which spec §5.1 leaves to the template because it is
not a per-field decision the way membership within the struct is (that one
is createInputMembers/updateInputMembers, in Go, in input.go).

Validate() error IS rendered here, right after each struct (issue #28,
spec §6.5): it is the method that actually enforces which members are
mandatory, plus the Go half of `max:` (spec §3.1), enum membership and the
explicit-null-on-a-non-nullable-member rule (spec §6.6). Which checks apply
to which member, and every message a check can emit, are decided in Go, in
validate.go's createValidateMembers/updateValidateMembers -- never
re-derived here from raw field flags, for the same §5.1 reason
createInputMembers/updateInputMembers exist. The per-member rendering itself
is factored into the "model/validate_member" template (templates/
model_validate.tmpl) because its shape does not depend on which input type
it runs against; IsCreate, already on each validateMember, carries the one
difference that does (spec §6.5's differing "missing" test).
*/ -}}
{{- define "model/entity.go" -}}
{{template "header" .}}
{{- with .Entity}}
// {{.GoName}} is the generated model for entity "{{comment .Name}}" (table "{{comment .Table}}").
//
// It is output only: the store fills it from a scanned row and a handler
// marshals it. Every field carries an explicit json tag naming its column, and
// no field is omitempty -- a NULL column must serialise as null rather than
// vanish from the object (spec §6.9.2).
type {{.GoName}} struct {
{{- range .Fields}}
	{{.GoName}} {{.GoType}} {{jsonTag .Column}}
{{- end}}
}
{{range enumFields .}}
// {{.EnumGoType}} is the generated type of the "{{comment .Name.Value}}" field.
// Its members are exactly the values the schema declares; the CHECK constraint
// in the migration is what enforces them in the database.
type {{.EnumGoType}} string

const (
{{- $enum := .EnumGoType}}
{{- range .EnumValues}}
	{{$enum}}{{.GoName}} {{$enum}} = {{goString .Name.Value}}
{{- end}}
)
{{end}}
{{- if .HasCreate}}

// {{.GoName}}CreateInput is the generated request body for {{.GoName}}'s create
// endpoint (spec §6.5). Every member is Optional[T], mandatory ones
// included: a bare value type cannot tell an empty body apart from an
// explicit null, the same trap a pointer falls into one type earlier
// (spec §6.5, §13). Validate (step 7) is what enforces which members are
// mandatory; this struct only says which members exist and whether each
// reaches the wire.
//
// A member tagged json:"-" is off the wire -- DisallowUnknownFields rejects
// an inbound key for it -- but a hook may still set it through Optional[T]'s
// Set/SetNull (spec §6.5, "off the wire, not out of the struct").
type {{.GoName}}CreateInput struct {
{{- range createInputMembers .}}
	{{.GoName}} Optional[{{.ValueGoType}}] {{.Tag}}
{{- end}}
}

// Validate reports whether in satisfies spec §6.5's "Question 2"
// (mandatory members), §3.1's `max:` and enum-membership checks, and §6.6's
// rule that an explicit null is rejected against a member whose column does
// not accept one. It runs before a transaction is opened (spec §6.5's fixed
// handler order: decode, Validate, open the transaction, BeforeX), so by the
// time BeforeCreate runs, every mandatory member is Present() and not
// IsNull().
func (in *{{.GoName}}CreateInput) Validate() error {
	fields := map[string]string{}
{{range createValidateMembers .}}{{template "model/validate_member" .}}
{{end -}}
	if len(fields) != 0 {
		return &ValidationError{Fields: fields}
	}
	return nil
}
{{- end}}
{{- if .HasUpdate}}

// {{.GoName}}UpdateInput is the generated request body for {{.GoName}}'s update
// endpoint (spec §6.5, §6.6). Absent means unchanged; Optional[T]'s IsNull is
// what distinguishes that from an explicit null, which PATCH semantics
// require and a pointer cannot express (spec §6.5, §13).
type {{.GoName}}UpdateInput struct {
{{- range updateInputMembers .}}
	{{.GoName}} Optional[{{.ValueGoType}}] {{.Tag}}
{{- end}}
}

// Validate reports whether in satisfies spec §6.5's "Question 2"
// (mandatory members), §3.1's `max:` and enum-membership checks, and §6.6's
// rule that an explicit null is rejected against a member whose column does
// not accept one. An absent member means "unchanged" (spec §6.6) and is
// never an error here, mandatory or not; only an explicit null against a
// mandatory member, or against one whose column is NOT NULL, is rejected.
func (in *{{.GoName}}UpdateInput) Validate() error {
	fields := map[string]string{}
{{range updateValidateMembers .}}{{template "model/validate_member" .}}
{{end -}}
	if len(fields) != 0 {
		return &ValidationError{Fields: fields}
	}
	return nil
}
{{- end}}
{{- end}}
{{- end -}}
